      "shortMessageHtmlLink": {
        "value": "<a data-pjax=\"true\" title=\"Turn the last two contracts into ports, and delete the layer that excused them\n\nBoth contracts could only be excused as core while they named something\noutside the domain. Settings and DiffChoices moved there in the last two\ncommits, so neither excuse is left.\n\nports/Settings.ts is the Store and nothing else: read, write, be told when\nanother tab wrote. The work over it went to app/settings.ts, which is where\na use case belongs — forgetful(), the store that keeps choices for as long\nas the page is open, rememberView, and chosenView with its quarter-second\npatience.\n\nports/Renderer.ts is what a diff renderer is, moved from src/diff whole.\nsrc/diff is now three files that each know something outside: the renderer\nand the two halves of Shiki. src/settings is two: Chrome&#39;s synced storage\nand its test.\n\nWhich means the `core` layer is gone from .sentrux/rules.toml. Eight named\nexceptions this afternoon, then four, then two, now none — the file\ndescribes a hexagon in globs alone, with no list of files that are somehow\nnot what their directory says.\n\nVerified: 971 tests pass, tsc --noEmit clean, oxlint clean, and no layer or\nboundary violation with the core layer removed, which is the part that\ncould have quietly gone wrong.\n\nThe one violation sentrux reports is still the four screens fanning out\npast fifteen. Measured before and after: 22, 18, 17, 17 either way, so\nsplitting one import into two did not move it.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor &lt;cursoragent@cursor.com&gt;\" class=\"Link--secondary\" href=\"/flazouh/githubpro/commit/3cd3cfeae3835e74b8c2c2175c9bc43f5eac9d96\">Turn the last two contracts into ports, and delete the layer that exc…</a>"
      }
    },
